  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass $m$ is attached to a spring (of spring constant $k$ ) and has a natural angular frequency $\\omega_0$. An external force $F(t)$ proportional to $\\cos \\omega t\\left(\\omega \\neq \\omega_0\\right)$ is applied to the oscillator. The time displacement of the oscillator will be proportional to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "BdjN4",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{\\omega_0^2-\\omega^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SlrgT",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{m\\left(\\omega_0^2-\\omega^2\\right)}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "eMYHt",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{m\\left(\\omega_0^2+\\omega^2\\right)}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SHP63",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{m}{\\omega_0^2+\\omega^2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For forced oscillations, the displacement is given by\n$$\n\\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{A} \\sin (\\omega \\mathrm{t}+\\phi) \\text { with } \\mathrm{A}=\\frac{\\mathrm{F}_0 / \\mathrm{m}}{\\omega_0^2-\\omega^2}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
